    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61723" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λᾰκ-ίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rent, rending</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				18.8
			</span></i> (pl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ . . ἐν πέπλοις πέσῃ λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					125
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπίτνω ξὺν λακίδι λίνοισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					131
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				903
			</span></i>: freq. in pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λακίδες ἐσθημάτων,
				ὑφασμάτων</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				835
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				28
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λακίδες πέπλων</span>
			<i>ragged</i> robes, <i>tatters</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				423
			</span></i>: in late Prose, of the <i>rent</i> or <i>gap</i> made in
			a ship by the enemy's beak, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				13.99
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				14.72
			</span></i>.</div>
